on remained unchanged.c. managers found that every process could switch immediately without any limit on the energy supply.d. the available renewable supply was enough for the drying stage, but not yet for every process.write a, b, c, or d - {#3} question 16.a. they were removed from the reduction plan because the drying stage used more coal.b. they were ranked for later review according to their coal use and the alternatives available.c. their coal use was assumed to be zero because they were not selected first.d. they were converted to renewable energy before any further comparison was made.write a, b, c, or d - {#4} question 17.a. this showed that only one process in any factory can produce climate emissions.b. as a result, managers no longer needed to monitor coal use in the other processes.c. the plan therefore started with the largest practical reduction while keeping other sources under review.d. the comparison proved that renewable energy could never replace fossil fuels.write a, b, c, or d - {#5}"
